},{"name":"Nick Xenophon","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10717","person_slug":"nick-xenophon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Nation-Building Funds Bill 2008 - Consideration of House of Representatives Message - Communications Fund","noes":7,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2008-12-04.395.5) introduced by Labor MP [Nick Sherry](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Nick_Sherry&mpc=Senate&house=senate). The motion was: \"_that the committee does not insist on amendments Nos (3), (4), (5), (8) and (10) to (13)._\"(See [here](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fsched%2Fr3099_sched_f32016d1-534a-4bf1-8cd8-da2f326aa9d1%22) for a schedule of the amendments made by the Senate to which the House of Representatives has disagreed. ) This motion was introduced after the House of Representatives rejected amendments that the Senate had agreed to while considering the bill.(Read more about the stages that a bill must pass through to become a law [here](http://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/making-a-law.html). Compare these stages to the progress of this bill [here](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r3099). ) These amendments related to the transfer of the Communications Fund.(Read more about the amendments in the debate over this motion [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2008-12-04.395.2). ) They opposed the proposal to transfer the balance of the Communications Fund to the [Building Australia Fund](http://www.finance.gov.au/investment-funds/NBF/BAF.html) to support the [National Broadband Network](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Broadband_Network). One senator, Liberal Senator [Alan Eggleston](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Alan_Eggleston&mpc=Senate&house=senate), rebelled and crossed the floor to vote 'no'.(Read more about what it means to cross the floor in our [FAQ Section](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/faq.php#rebelandfree).) Read more about the bill [here](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/R","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1590","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2008-12-04/10"}
